  "implemented": [
    "Opt-in SessionPayloadLimits on ordinary request/reply serialized JSON bytes; defaults preserve existing large-history payloads.",
    "Local request checks precede admission; a cheap bounded lower-bound walk precedes the stopping counting serializer.",
    "Incoming declared lengths are checked before payload spooling/decoding.",
    "Separate 64 KiB control request/reply budget; configured reply caps below it are rejected before process launch.",
    "Local typed PayloadLimitExceeded cannot be forged merely by a legacy remote error string.",
    "Cleanup release_reply preserves the actual operation/cleanup receipt; terminal peer size failures retain typed cause through cleanup and close and reap the process.",
    "Server reply rejection preserves the legacy wire error and control lane; reader size failures survive subsequent writer failures."
  ],
  "remaining_limits": [
    "Limits are opt-in; this checkpoint does not apply native-search budgets or change existing storage defaults.",
    "Limits cover logical serialized bodies, not total process memory or caller allocations already used to construct a Value.",
    "The wire format and protocol version remain unchanged.",
    "No installed search-provider integration, separate search-package build, new CLI/App Server binary, or GUI runtime gate is established here."
  ]
